  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Arizona received $25.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 16,210 awards with an average award size of $1.6M, and obligations were up 9.2% year over year. The Department of Defense and the Department of Homeland Security account for the largest shares, with $17.9B and $6.2B respectively. RAYTHEON COMPANY, TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP, and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO are the largest vendors by obligations, with $8.1B, $4.7B, and $4.5B respectively. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction are the top industries, with $6.4B and $6.1B in obligations respectively. These totals are fiscal year to date and are partial for the current year. Historical fiscal-year totals show growth from $16.5B in FY21 to $25.5B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $15.3B in FY22, $19.8B in FY23, $18B in FY24, and $23.3B in FY25.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Arizona trended recently?",
        "body": "FY26 to date obligations are $25.5B, up 9.2% year over year. Fiscal-year totals rose from $16.5B in FY21 to $25.5B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $15.3B in FY22, $19.8B in FY23, $18B in FY24, and $23.3B in FY25. Award volume stands at 16,210 and the average award size is $1.6M, reflecting both larger and more numerous obligations this fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal spending in Arizona?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads buying with $17.9B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $6.2B. RAYTHEON COMPANY is the largest vendor with $8.1B, followed by TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP with $4.7B and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO with $4.5B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing ($6.4B) and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction ($6.1B) are the largest industries by obligations."
      }
    ]
